  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Publishes the public CreateUseSiteOptionsMonitor<TOptions> API for isolated middleware use-site overrides. It rebuilds the normal registered options/configuration baseline, runs registered PostConfigure steps, applies the local use-site override afterwards, runs registered validation, supports configuration reload and OnChange, reapplies the local override after reload, and leaves global options unchanged. Also includes one-record-per-request traffic logging on ASP.NET Core HTTP Logging, shared NetLib IP normalization in client-network features, Eigenverft.NetLib.Infrastructure 1.0.20264.61091, and the neutral Eigenverft package icon. Adds WebLib HSTS helpers over ASP.NET Core's native HSTS implementation with a 180-day default, Hsts configuration binding, and optional code override. Adds RequestTrafficShaping startup options/JSON binding with a native per-client TokenBucketRateLimiter followed by a shared server-wide TokenBucketRateLimiter and optional global concurrency limiting. PerClient.Enabled and ServerWide.Enabled both default to true. ServerWide uses WebLib starting defaults of 10,000 requests/second, 10,000 burst capacity, and a 10,000-request bounded queue; these are tunable infrastructure starting values rather than capacity guarantees. Both token-bucket option groups validate BurstSize >= RequestsPerSecond for the current one-second replenishment mapping. The earlier development name FloodProtection was fully renamed to RequestTrafficShaping; the old development API and configuration section are intentionally not retained and no compatibility aliases are provided.",
